== NEXT: Phase 0b step 3 - engine-owned state (D18) ==
Why: today attention receives a raw per-layer cache plus BatchMeta.cache_context and writes into
the cache itself, and the runtime builds those caches separately from the page bookkeeping. The
target (GOAL_ARCHITECTURE section 4, rule 3) is: a mixer only DECLARES what state it needs; one
engine object, the StateManager, allocates it, owns every request's length, and gives each layer
a small view for the current batch. Later state kinds (MLA latent KV, KDA recurrent state, sliding
windows) then plug in as new specs + storage, with no change to attention or the runtime.
Behavior is unchanged: same storage, same kernels, same numbers.
Done when: tests/test_state_contracts.py passes (CPU: runs on the laptop), the two state tests in
tests/test_model_contracts.py pass (CPU), and the DEFERRED GPU list passes.

[ ] 3.1 Shared state types - core/state.py (new; imports nothing from model/ or inference/)
      FullKVSpec(num_kv_heads: int, head_dim: int): frozen dataclass; both must be positive ints
        (bools rejected) else ValueError. Means: per request, per token, K and V of [num_kv_heads,
        head_dim]. Class attribute kind = "full_kv".
      PagedKVRead: frozen dataclass, everything a paged-attention kernel needs to read one layer:
        k, v              [num_blocks, block_size, H_kv, D]
        k_scales, v_scales [num_blocks, block_size, H_kv], or None when the storage is unquantized
        block_table       [max_slots, max_blocks_per_request] int32 (the allocator's full table)
        slots             [B] long, each request's slot row in block_table
        context_lengths   [B], committed tokens + this batch's tokens, per request
        block_size        int
      FullKVView: runtime_checkable Protocol with
        append(k: [T, H_kv, D], v: [T, H_kv, D]) -> None   writes this batch's tokens
        read() -> PagedKVRead
      Done: test_full_kv_spec_* in tests/test_state_contracts.py.

[ ] 3.2 Engine state owner - inference/page_allocator.py, inference/state_manager.py
      page_allocator.py: rename cache_manager.py -> page_allocator.py and KVCacheManager ->
        PageAllocator; keep its slot/page bookkeeping and CacheCapacityError. Delete
        initialize_cache, append_request, create_container and CacheContainer (replaced below).
        Add truncate(request_id, length): requires 0 <= length <= current length (ValueError
        otherwise); lowers the host and device lengths; the pages stay reserved.
      state_manager.py:
        StateSnapshot(request_id: int, length: int): frozen dataclass.
        PagedKVView(storage, blocks, offsets, read): append(k, v) calls
          storage.append_kv(blocks, offsets, k, v); read() returns the PagedKVRead.
        StateManager(layer_specs: list[list[spec]], config: KVCacheConfig, device):
          owns one PageAllocator built from config, and storage[layer][j] = a PagedKVCache for
          each FullKVSpec (dtype config.kv_cache_dtype, scales config.kv_scale_dtype).
          can_reserve(capacity) -> bool    a free slot AND enough free pages, right now
          fits_in_pool(capacity) -> bool   capacity <= max_seq_len AND its pages <= all pages
          reserve(request_id, capacity)    1st call takes a slot; later calls grow capacity;
                                           all-or-nothing (CacheCapacityError, nothing taken)
          commit(request_ids, num_tokens)  = today's advance_batch
          seq_len(request_id) -> int
          truncate(request_id, length)
          snapshot(request_id) -> StateSnapshot(request_id, current length)
          restore(snapshot)                truncate back to snapshot.length; ValueError if the
                                           request now has fewer tokens than that
          free(request_id); request_ids() -> list[int]; clear()
          layer_states(request_ids, cu_seqlens, token_positions) -> list[tuple[view, ...]]
            one tuple per layer, one view per spec of that layer. Locations and context lengths
            are computed ONCE per batch and shared by every layer's view. Reads no device values
            (no .item()/.tolist() on GPU tensors). context_lengths = device seq_lens[slots] +
            this batch's per-request token counts, so call it BEFORE commit.
          Unknown request -> KeyError.
        Why snapshot/restore are just lengths: K/V is append-only, so rolling back = forgetting
          the tail. Recurrent kinds (KDA, later) will copy their state in snapshot instead; the
          API stays the same.
      paged_kv_cache.py: unchanged (it IS the full-KV storage).
      Done: all of tests/test_state_contracts.py (CPU).

[ ] 3.3 Model side - core/interfaces.py, core/batch_meta.py, model/attention.py, model/moe/moe.py,
        model/decoder_block.py, model/model.py, kernals/decode_attention.py
      SequenceMixer protocol: add state_specs(self) -> list (empty list = stateless);
        forward(x, meta, state): state = tuple of views in state_specs() order, or None in training.
      GQA:
        state_specs() -> [FullKVSpec(config.num_kv_heads, config.head_dim)]
        rename the input back from `state` to `x` (`state` is now the views argument; the residual
          state is a third, different thing). Same for MoE's input.
        train: state is None. prefill: (kv,) = state; flash attention on this batch's k/v, then
          kv.append(k_rope, v). decode: kv.append(k_rope, v), then
          decode_attention_wrapper(q_rope, kv.read()).
      decode_attention_wrapper(q, kv: PagedKVRead): take k, v, scales, block_table, slots,
        context_lengths, block_size from kv (instead of paged_kv_cache + cache_batch_context);
        quantized = kv.k_scales is not None. Kernel body unchanged.
      DecoderBlock.forward(state, residual, meta, layer_state=None): mixer(x, meta, layer_state).
      TransformerLM.forward(meta, states=None): states[i] goes to block i; None in training.
        TransformerLM.state_specs() -> [block.mixer.state_specs() for each block].
      BatchMeta: remove cache_context and its validation rules (D14 marked it transitional).
      Done: test_gqa_declares_its_kv_state, test_model_state_specs_list_every_layer (CPU).

[ ] 3.4 Runtime - inference/runtime.py
      __init__: self.state_manager = StateManager(model.state_specs(), kvcache_config, device),
        replacing initialize_cache / cache_manager / paged_kv_caches.
      required_capacity: state_manager.fits_in_pool(capacity) instead of counting blocks.
      admit_waiting: state_manager.can_reserve(capacity), then reserve(request_id, capacity).
      run_batch: states = state_manager.layer_states(request_ids, batch.cu_seqlens,
        batch.token_positions) BEFORE the model; model(batch_meta, states); commit(...) where
        advance_batch was; free(request_id) for finished requests.
      error path: free every request in state_manager.request_ids().
      Done: tests/test_inference.py (CPU). Claude first updates its stand-in model to the new
        signature (see 3.5).

[ ] 3.5 Tell Claude (push first). Claude then updates the tests that use the old cache API
      (test_inference, test_attention, test_kv_cache*, test_transformer_lm, test_decode_attention,
      the cache_context cases in test_core_contracts), and marks D18 Implemented.


